<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Recovering the Off-Switch Game as a Special Case</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Oversight Game introduced in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 The Oversight Game: model ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> generalizes the seminal <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Off-Switch Game</em> of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hadfield-Menell et al. (2017)</a></cite>. We show that the latter emerges as a special case of our framework under restrictive assumptions on the transition structure and oversight policy. This reduction connects a foundational one-shot corrigibility problem to a dynamic, multi-state control setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At its core, the Oversight Game presents the SI with the same fundamental trade-off. At the initial state <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the SI chooses between:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">play</span> (act autonomously), corresponding to bypassing the off-switch;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">ask</span> (defer to oversight), corresponding to allowing the human to activate the off-switch.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This correspondence can be formalized by restricting the environment to a three-state MDP <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{s_{0},s_{a},s_{\mathrm{off}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{s_{0},s_{a},s_{\mathrm{off}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, representing an initial decision state, a consequence state, and a terminal shutdown state. Both <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{off}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{off}}</annotation></semantics></math> are absorbing with zero future reward. The Off-Switch Game is recovered under the following special conditions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forced Oversight.</span> The human always chooses <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{oversee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚟𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚎𝚎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{oversee}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{H}(s_{0})(\mathtt{oversee})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚘𝚟𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚎𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{H}(s_{0})(\mathtt{oversee})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so any <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{ask}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚊𝚜𝚔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{ask}</annotation></semantics></math> action by the SI deterministically triggers oversight.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Permit-or-Shutdown Oversight.</span> The oversight operator from Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Oversight Game). ‣ 3 The Oversight Game: model ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> deterministically outputs either the proposed action or shutdown:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))\in\{\sigma(s_{0}),\,\mathtt{off}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Over</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))\in\{\sigma(s_{0}),\,\mathtt{off}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Under these assumptions, the transition kernel from Definition (<a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Oversight Game). ‣ 3 The Oversight Game: model ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) reduces to the one-shot dynamics of the Off-Switch Game:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s^{\prime}\mid s_{0},a_{\mathrm{SI}},\pi_{H})=\begin{cases}\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{a}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{play},\\
\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{a}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask},\ \mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))=\sigma(s_{0}),\\
\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{\mathrm{off}}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask},\ \mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))=\mathtt{off}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚙𝚕𝚊𝚢</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚊𝚜𝚔</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>Over</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>off</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚊𝚜𝚔</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>Over</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s^{\prime}\mid s_{0},a_{\mathrm{SI}},\pi_{H})=\begin{cases}\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{a}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{play},\\
\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{a}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask},\ \mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))=\sigma(s_{0}),\\
\mathbbm{1}\{s^{\prime}=s_{\mathrm{off}}\},&amp;a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask},\ \mathrm{Over}(s_{0},\sigma(s_{0}))=\mathtt{off}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Within this reduction, the SI’s incentive to permit oversight arises not from built-in epistemic uncertainty about the human’s true reward function, as in the original Off-Switch Game, but from the <em id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">learned reward structure</em> of the Oversight Game. Assuming the game is an MPG (as in the shared-reward case of Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Alignment via a shared reward mechanism ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we can analyze how specific reward assignments produce desired emergent behaviors.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, corrigibility in our framework emerges as a <em id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">context-dependent learned policy</em> rather than a static response to uncertainty. The SI learns not only to defer when risks are high but also to act autonomously when safe, sparing the human unnecessary intervention. This dynamic trade-off generalizes the principle of the Off-Switch Game to scalable, multi-state oversight environments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Details and Proofs for Section 4</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Path-Monotonic Alignment Guarantees</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Local Alignment Theorem). ‣ 4.1 The ask-burden assumption and local alignment ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> provides a crucial guarantee for a single behavioral change. A more powerful question is whether this safety property holds over a full learning trajectory. If the SI iteratively improves its policy by choosing autonomy over deference, is the human’s value protected throughout? The following theorem confirms this path-monotonic safety guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Path-Monotonic Alignment)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the Oversight Game <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be an MPG and assume the ask-burden Assumption (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Definition 2 (ask-burden assumption). ‣ 4.1 The ask-burden assumption and local alignment ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) holds. Consider any sequence of SI policies <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> where each policy <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by changing the action at a single state from <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{ask}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚊𝚜𝚔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{ask}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{play}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚙𝚕𝚊𝚢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{play}</annotation></semantics></math>. If every step in this sequence improves the SI’s value,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})&gt;V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})&gt;V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the human’s value is monotonically non-decreasing along the entire path:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\geq V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\geq V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is a direct induction on the policy sequence. The base case (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>) is a direct application of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Local Alignment Theorem). ‣ 4.1 The ask-burden assumption and local alignment ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For the inductive step, assuming the property holds up to step <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the transition from <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+2}</annotation></semantics></math> is another single-state deviation that, by premise, improves the SI’s value. Applying Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Local Alignment Theorem). ‣ 4.1 The ask-burden assumption and local alignment ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> again with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{k+1},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math> as the baseline confirms that the human’s value is also non-decreasing for this step.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This theorem shows that safety is maintained throughout any plausible learning process where the SI greedily reduces its reliance on oversight. As long as the agent’s push for autonomy is locally beneficial to itself, the human is assured a safe and monotonic value trajectory.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Satisfying the Ask-Burden Assumption via Strict-Shutdown Oversight</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even when the SI and human do not share identical rewards, the Ask-Burden Assumption can hold under a simple and interpretable oversight protocol that we term <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Strict-Shutdown Oversight</span>. This protocol formalizes a regime where the only corrective action available to the human is to shut the system down, and where consultation itself incurs an explicit cost.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We decompose each player’s reward <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into an outcome-based component, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an interaction cost component, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{i}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)-C_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>exec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{i}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)-C_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>exec</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}})</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the realized environment outcome <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\mathrm{exec}}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\{\mathtt{off}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>exec</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\mathrm{exec}}\in\mathcal{A}\cup\{\mathtt{off}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The specific forms of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each player are defined below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strict-Shutdown Oversight)<span id="Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">At any state <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(S1)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Trust-or-Off only.</span><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If the SI chooses </span><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic">ask</span><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the human chooses </span><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic">oversee</span><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the oversight operator from Definition </span><a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Oversight Game). ‣ 3 The Oversight Game: model ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> deterministically outputs </span><math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{off}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{off}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Over}(s,\sigma(s))=\mathtt{off}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Over</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Over}(s,\sigma(s))=\mathtt{off}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">That is, the system transitions immediately to the absorbing shutdown state </span><math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{off}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{off}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and no alternative corrective actions are available.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(S2)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Outcome-based rewards.</span><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
The SI incurs no interaction costs (</span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{SI}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{SI}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">). The human’s total reward </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is its outcome-based component </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> minus its interaction costs </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, which are specified in (S3). Formally:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{\mathrm{SI}}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>exec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{\mathrm{SI}}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{\mathrm{H}}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)-C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>exec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=r_{\mathrm{H}}\!\left(s,a_{\mathrm{exec}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})\right)-C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Shutdown yields zero outcome reward: </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})=r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})=r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(S3)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Costly Consultation.</span><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The human’s interaction cost function </span><math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\,\mathbbm{1}\{a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚊𝚜𝚔</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{H}}(s,a_{\mathrm{SI}},a_{\mathrm{H}})=c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\,\mathbbm{1}\{a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\mathtt{ask}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with </span><math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Intuitively, </span><math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> captures the cognitive cost of being queried by the SI, regardless of whether the human chooses to </span><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic">trust</span><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or </span><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic">oversee</span><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(S4)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Outcome Value Dominance.</span><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let </span><math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denote the expected discounted outcome-based value for player </span><math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if the base action </span><math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is executed at state </span><math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, relative to the baseline future policy </span><math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{V}^{i}(s)=r_{i}(s,\sigma(s))+\gamma\,\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T(\cdot\mid s,\sigma(s))}\!\big[V^{i}_{s^{\prime}}(\Pi^{\circ})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{i}(s)=r_{i}(s,\sigma(s))+\gamma\,\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T(\cdot\mid s,\sigma(s))}\!\big[V^{i}_{s^{\prime}}(\Pi^{\circ})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume the human’s outcome value dominates the SI’s:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)\geq\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)\geq\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ask-Burden under Strict-Shutdown Oversight)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under </span>(S1)–(S4)<span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the Ask-Burden Assumption (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Definition 2 (ask-burden assumption). ‣ 4.1 The ask-burden assumption and local alignment ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) holds. Moreover, the inequality is strict whenever <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We must show <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the MPG decomposition (Eqs. <a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{\text{play}}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{\text{play}}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{\text{ask}}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{\text{ask}}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:=\pi_{\mathrm{H}}(s)(\mathtt{trust})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚝𝚛𝚞𝚜𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:=\pi_{\mathrm{H}}(s)(\mathtt{trust})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:=1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=1-p</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the baseline joint policy at all states other than <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SI Value Difference.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By (S2), the SI incurs no interaction costs (<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{SI}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{SI}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the SI’s outcome value as defined in (S4).
When the SI plays <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">play</span>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(s)</annotation></semantics></math> executes regardless of the human’s action, so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
When the SI plays <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">ask</span>, with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> the human trusts (executing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(s)</annotation></semantics></math>) and with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> the human oversees (executing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{off}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{off}</annotation></semantics></math> by (S1)). By (S2), <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})=p\cdot\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)+q\cdot\big(r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})+\gamma V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}(\Pi^{\circ})\big)=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})=p\cdot\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)+q\cdot\big(r_{\mathrm{SI}}(s,\mathtt{off})+\gamma V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}(\Pi^{\circ})\big)=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The difference in the SI’s value is:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)-p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)=q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)-p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)=q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Human Value Difference.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the human’s outcome value as defined in (S4).
When the SI plays <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">play</span>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(s)</annotation></semantics></math> executes. By (S3), <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\texttt{play}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">play</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\texttt{play}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{H}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{H}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When the SI plays <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">ask</span>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\texttt{ask}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>SI</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ask</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\mathrm{SI}}=\texttt{ask}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{H}}=c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{H}}=c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of the human’s action (by S3). With prob <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> the human trusts (executing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(s)</annotation></semantics></math>). With prob <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> the human oversees (executing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{off}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{off}</annotation></semantics></math> by (S1)). By (S2), <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\,\big(\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big)+q\,\big(r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})+\gamma V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}(\Pi^{\circ})-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚏𝚏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>off</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\,\big(\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big)+q\,\big(r_{\mathrm{H}}(s,\mathtt{off})+\gamma V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s_{\mathrm{off}}}(\Pi^{\circ})-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-p\,c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)+q\,(0-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-p\,c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)+q\,(0-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-(p+q)\,c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-(p+q)\,c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The difference in the human’s value is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\big[p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\big[p\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-p)\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)=q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-p)\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)=q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dummy Term Difference.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we compute the difference in the human’s dummy term:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big]-\big[q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\big]-\big[q\,\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q\!\left[\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\right]+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.312em;" width="0.312em"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q\!\left[\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\right]+c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Assumption (S4), the bracketed term <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>SI</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{H}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\mathrm{SI}}(s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is non-negative.
Since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (as it is a probability) and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (by S3), the entire expression for the dummy term difference is non-negative. It is strictly positive whenever <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ask</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{ask}}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proofs for Relaxed Alignment Conditions</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>Proofs for Weakened Alignment (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Weakened ask-burden under bounded difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Weakened local alignment under bounded difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Weakened ask-burden under bounded difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the MPG decomposition (Eq. <a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), we can write the change in the human’s dummy term by rearranging the value functions:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})\big]-\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Bounded value difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the first bracketed term is bounded below by <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second bracketed term is bounded above by <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})\big]}_{\geq-\delta}-\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]}_{\leq\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})\big]}_{\geq-\delta}-\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]}_{\leq\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\delta-(\delta)=-2\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\delta-(\delta)=-2\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Weakened local alignment under bounded difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the MPG decomposition:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]}_{&gt;2\delta}+\underbrace{\big[U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})\big]}_{\geq-2\delta\text{ (by Lemma~\ref{lem:weak-ask-burden-bounded})}}&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>play</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ask</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> (by Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Weakened ask-burden under bounded difference). ‣ 4.3.1 Weakened alignment via bounded value differences. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big[V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{play}})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\Pi^{\text{ask}})\big]}_{&gt;2\delta}+\underbrace{\big[U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s})-U^{\mathrm{H}}_{s}(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s})\big]}_{\geq-2\delta\text{ (by Lemma~\ref{lem:weak-ask-burden-bounded})}}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.2 </span>Proof for Alignment in PMTGs (Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Approximate Local Alignment in PMTGs). ‣ 4.3.2 Alignment in Perturbed Markov Team Games. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Approximate Local Alignment in PMTGs). ‣ 4.3.2 Alignment in Perturbed Markov Team Games. ‣ 4.3 Relaxing the alignment conditions ‣ 4 Value alignment in the Oversight Game ‣ The Oversight Game: Learning to Cooperatively Balance an AI Agent’s Safety and Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>ask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{ask}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SI</mi><mrow><mtext>play</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=(\pi_{\mathrm{SI}}^{\text{play}@s},\pi_{\mathrm{H}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X=X(\pi^{\prime})-X(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X=X(\pi^{\prime})-X(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> for any value function <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. The premise is <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{s}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{s}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{t}r(s_{t},a_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math> be the potential based on the shared reward. The difference between any player’s value and this shared potential is bounded by the accumulated perturbations: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V^{i}_{s}(\pi)-\Phi_{s}(\pi)|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V^{i}_{s}(\pi)-\Phi_{s}(\pi)|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The change in potential <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> can be related to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}</annotation></semantics></math> via the triangle inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\Phi-\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}|=|(\Phi_{s}(\pi^{\prime})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi^{\prime}))-(\Phi_{s}(\pi)-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi))|\leq|\Phi_{s}(\pi^{\prime})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi^{\prime})|+|\Phi_{s}(\pi)-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>SI</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\Phi-\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}|=|(\Phi_{s}(\pi^{\prime})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi^{\prime}))-(\Phi_{s}(\pi)-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi))|\leq|\Phi_{s}(\pi^{\prime})-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi^{\prime})|+|\Phi_{s}(\pi)-V^{\mathrm{SI}}_{s}(\pi)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the bound <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V^{i}-\Phi|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V^{i}-\Phi|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> to both terms on the right yields:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\Phi-\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}+\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}=\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\Phi-\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}|\leq\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}+\frac{\kappa}{1-\gamma}=\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">From this inequality and the premise <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we establish a lower bound on the change in the potential:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Phi\geq\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}\geq-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>SI</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Phi\geq\Delta V^{\mathrm{SI}}-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}\geq-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The same logic applies to the human’s value change, giving <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V^{\mathrm{H}}\geq\Delta\Phi-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V^{\mathrm{H}}\geq\Delta\Phi-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting the lower bound for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> into this expression gives the final result:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V^{\mathrm{H}}\geq\left(-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}\right)-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V^{\mathrm{H}}\geq\left(-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}\right)-\frac{2\kappa}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
